    Merge branch 'reorganize-forge-gui' into 'master'
    
    Reorganize "forge-gui*" projects
    
    This is just a first iteration. Eventually, it will be easier to only leave in "forge-gui" GUI-related classes, with the rest moved into a new "forge-common" or something like that.
    
    Before this MR, all packages within "forge-gui" were at the same hierarchical level. Then, there was no straightforward way to realize which package was more closely related to which other one(s).
    
    In this first iteration, I simply grouped them based on their collaborations:
    
    I did three commits:
    
    1) refactor: group local instance-related packages
    
      I moved the following packages into forge.localinstance:
      - achievements,
      - assets,
      - properties
    
    2) refactor: group game modes-related packages
    
      I moved the following packages into forge.gamemodes:
      - gauntlet,
      - limited,
      - match,
      - net,
      - planarconquest,
      - puzzle,
      - quest,
      - tournament
    
    3) refactor: group gui-related packages
    
      I moved the following packages into forge.gui:
      - card,
      - control,
      - download,
      - error,
      - events,
      - interfaces
      - util
    
    In every step, I also moved some classes that were definitely into one of those groups. Of course, there are still many classes that should be split:  I  plan to do this later on.
    
    See merge request core-developers/forge!4106

